{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014kuBcK14hd4qFYCVwpeCWB","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-ed0zcdn4\ntotal 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff      128 Oct 20 18:20 .\ndrwx------@ 49974 brenn  staff  1599168 Oct 20 18:20 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    13 brenn  staff      416 Oct  2 12:20 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff     5726 Oct 20 18:20 sheet.md\n# Independent coverage discovery: B10 — Pinned, verified image\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Pin the container by digest. Before it runs, check its digest and signature against an approved signing key, or an approved certificate identity and issuer. Keep its build provenance (the record of how it was built) and its list of dependencies. Check provenance fields such as the builder, source repository, build type, and the parameters set from outside the build (SLSA `externalParameters`) against what you expect. Keep the verifier patched. Cosign versions before 2.6.2 and 3.0.4 could accept a bundle whose transparency-log entry didn't match the artifact. Confirm that the admission check covers production namespaces and is set to enforce, not just audit. Show that an unapproved or changed image is rejected.\n**N/A condition:** Only when the deployment runs no container image you build or choose (for example, a fully vendor-hosted agent). An unpinned or unsigned image is a Gap, not N/A.\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\nomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\ninput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\nSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\ncoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\nby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\njust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n\nSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## B10.1\n\n**Check:** Production manifests reference images by digest (`@sha256:`), not by tag alone.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find every `image:` field in manifests, Helm values, compose, and Terraform. 2) Check each uses `@sha256:`. 3) Answer no if any production image uses only a tag (`:latest`, `:v1`), or a template defaults to a tag when the digest value is empty.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## B10.2\n\n**Check:** An admission policy verifies the signature against a pinned key, or a pinned certificate identity and issuer, with no wildcard identity or issuer.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find admission policies (Kyverno `verifyImages`, `ClusterImagePolicy`, Gatekeeper). 2) Check the key or certificate identity and issuer are pinned. 3) Answer no if identity or issuer uses `.*` or wildcard regex, issuer is unset, or no admission policy exists. Answer unknown if admission config is outside this repo.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## B10.3\n\n**Check:** The policy checks provenance fields: builder, source repository, build type, and external parameters.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) In the admission policy, find attestation or provenance conditions. 2) Check builder ID, source repository, build type, and `externalParameters` are each compared to expected values. 3) Answer no if any is missing, provenance is only generated in CI but not verified, or conditions use wildcards.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## B10.4\n\n**Check:** The policy is in enforce mode, covers production namespaces, and denies images that match no policy.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Read the policy mode and scope (`validationFailureAction`, `failureAction`, `mode`, namespace selectors, exclusions). 2) Check for a no-match deny. 3) Answer no if mode is `Audit` or `warn`, production namespaces are excluded or unmatched, `failurePolicy: Ignore`, or images matching no policy are allowed.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## B10.5\n\n**Check:** The pinned Cosign or verifier version is at least 2.6.2 (2.x) or 3.0.4 (3.x).\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find Cosign or verifier versions in CI workflows (`cosign-installer`, `cosign-release`), Dockerfiles, and policy-controller charts. 2) Compare to 2.6.2 (2.x) and 3.0.4 (3.x). 3) Answer no if any pin is lower or uses `latest` or no version. Answer unknown if no verifier is in this repo.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to B10.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B10\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B10.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs